{"version": 2, "width": 110, "height": 24, "timestamp": 1795521697, "title": "design/pricing-page \u00b7 ambitious run 4", "env": {"TERM": "xterm-256color"}, "theme": {"fg": "#d8dee9", "bg": "#1e1f1c", "palette": "#272822:#f92672:#a6e22e:#f4bf75:#66d9ef:#ae81ff:#a1efe4:#f8f8f2:#75715e:#f92672:#a6e22e:#f4bf75:#66d9ef:#ae81ff:#a1efe4:#f9f8f5"}}
[0.0, "o", "\u001b[?25l"]
[0.0, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m❯ Design a pricing page for an invoicing app for freelancers, as a single web page\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[40.999, "o", "\r\n\u001b[32m⏺\u001b[0m \u001b[1mWrote 1 file\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[90m  ⎿  Write(<workspace>/pricing.html)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[46.465, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ I built the pricing page as one self-contained file, `<workspace>/pricing.html`. I haven't opened it in a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  browser, so the layout and the billing toggle are untested.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  I invented the product name (Ledgerly), the prices, the testimonial and the \"40,000+ freelancers\" figure.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Swap in your own.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **What's on the page**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Hero and billing toggle:** a short headline, then a Monthly/Yearly switch with a \"2 months free\" tag.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Yearly is selected by default, and the toggle updates the prices and billing notes.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Three plans:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Starter:** $0, free forever.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Freelancer:** $10 a month billed yearly, or $12 billed monthly. It's the highlighted \"Most popular\"\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  plan.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Studio:** $24 a month billed yearly, or $29 billed monthly. It's for small teams.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Trust strip:** free trial, no setup fees, data export and a money-back guarantee.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Comparison table:** grouped into Invoicing, Money, and Team & support.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Testimonial, FAQ and final call to action:** six FAQ questions, including \"Do you take a cut of my\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  payments?\" and what happens if you go over the Starter limits.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Design choices**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Look:** a warm off-white background with a green accent and system fonts. It switches to a dark theme\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  automatically.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Responsive and accessible:** the plans stack on mobile and the table scrolls sideways if it's too wide.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  It has keyboard focus rings, `aria-pressed` on the toggle, and it respects reduced-motion settings.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Dependencies:** no frameworks or external assets, only a few lines of vanilla JavaScript for the toggle.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  The call-to-action buttons all point to `#`, so you'll need to add your signup URLs.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[46.915, "o", "\r\n\u001b[33m⚑ Stop hook: Before you finish, unless the task was trivial (a typo, a rename, a one-line answer), end with\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m  one question, using AskUserQuestion when it's available:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  ⎿  … +5 lines of instructions\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[50.998, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ I'd push the page further in three ways:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  1. **Check it in a browser.** I'd screenshot it at desktop and mobile widths, in light and dark, and fix\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  whatever looks off. This is cheap, about a tenth of what the first build cost.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  2. **Add a currency and annual-savings touch.** The toggle would show the exact yearly savings per plan, and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  a currency selector would switch the prices. This is small, about the same cost as the check.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  3. **Add polish.** That means a favicon, Open Graph tags, subtle scroll-in animation, and a \"Contact us\"\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Enterprise row for larger clients. It's moderate, about a quarter of the first build.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Do you want to push on?\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Push it further, step by step:** you see the result of each step and reply before the next one.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Push it further:** the steps run straight through.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Stop here.**\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[57.162, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m❯ Push it further.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
