[367.114, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ The page now answers the four worries in the first screen and tells each visitor which plan fits them. I\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  checked it by rendering it at real widths: a 1280px desktop view and a true 390px phone view, using an\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  iframe because headless Chrome won't go below about 500px.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Step report**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Did**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Worries up front:** four short cards under the headline cover no hidden fees, no lock-in, data safety,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  and looking professional. They sit above the plans on every screen size.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Plan picker:** each plan now has a \"Best for\" line in a freelancer's own words (side projects, full-time\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  freelancers, you plus subcontractors). The vague taglines are gone. Each button also has a small line under\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  it, such as \"No card needed · cancel anytime\".\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Honest branding:** Starter invoices carry a small \"Sent with Ledgerly\" footer, and paid plans remove it.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  This appears in the plan list, the comparison table, and the FAQ.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Data section:** I added a \"Your data\" group to the comparison table and a \"How is my data protected?\"\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  FAQ entry.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **FAQ order:** the first four questions now match the four worries (fees, leaving, data, branding), with\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  the fees answer open by default.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Placeholder cleanup:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - I removed the \"40,000+ freelancers\" claim and the old trust strip, which repeated the worry cards.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - I rewrote the testimonial to speak to the worries.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - Two spots are marked with `PLACEHOLDER` comments for you to replace: the testimonial, and the data-\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  protection claim (encryption and daily backups). Confirm that claim against your real setup before launch,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  because I invented it.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Found**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - On desktop, the headline, worries, and the first plan prices are all in view, and the buttons start at the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  bottom edge.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - On phone, my first version let the worry cards push the plans far below the fold. On small screens I cut\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  the cards to titles only, so the plans now start in the first screen. The cost is that on phone each worry\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  shows only its short title; the full answers are in the FAQ.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - A stylesheet ordering mistake made my phone fix not apply at first. I fixed it by moving the rule to the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  end.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Changed course**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Eyebrow:** I dropped the \"Simple pricing, no surprises\" tag to save vertical space.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Headline:** it changed from \"Get paid faster. Pay for less.\" to \"Pick the plan that fits how you work.\"\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  This fits the plan-picking goal better, but it is a copy change you may want to veto.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Screenshots:** I took one screenshot sheet per round and removed the temporary file from the project\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  folder afterwards.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  ▪ Step 3/8 done\u001b[0m\r\n"]
