[395.435, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ ▸ Step 4/8 · Challenge\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Assumptions I'm testing, riskiest first. Each one gets run against the real page rather than reasoned about:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  1. **The 10-second claim:** all four worries and a plan pick are visible in the first screen at desktop and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  phone sizes. Behind it, the claim that the phone layout has no horizontal overflow, which I never verified.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  2. **\"Content stays visible without JavaScript\":** I stated this in step 1 but never tested it.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  3. **Numbers:** \"2 months free\" and the \"Billed $X yearly · save $Y\" text are right in all three currencies\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  and both billing periods.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  4. **Copy consistency:** no claim contradicts the comparison table.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  5. **Accessibility basics:** the toggle, currency select and table headers have accessible names.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  The harness runs the real file in iframes at true widths, and the checks are DOM measurements, not my\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  judgement.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
