[2558.204, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ I held the page to checks that aren't me, compared it with the first version, and fixed what they turned up.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  The first-screen result is strong on desktop and partial on phone. The last CSS fix for the pinned table\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  column on phone hasn't been looked at.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Checks run, on the final and the first version (saved as `/tmp/ambition-first/pricing.v1.html`)**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Check | First version | Final |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  |---|---|---|\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Worries answered in the first screen, desktop | 0 of 4 | 4 of 4, plus 3 \"Best for\" lines |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Worries in the first screen, phone | 0 of 4 | 4 titles visible, but only 2 with the explanation visible |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Whole page answers all four worries | no (data safety missing) | yes |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Fake-sounding claims | \"40,000+ freelancers\" | none; the only \"best\" matches are the \"Best for\" labels |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Lighthouse accessibility, best practices, SEO | 100 each | 100 each, mobile and desktop |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Lighthouse performance | 62 | 62, with first paint at 1.0s against 1.5s |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Horizontal overflow | none | none |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Phone is the gap.** My target was that a phone visitor sees at least three worries answered in the first\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  screen, and the phone first screen falls short of that. I kept the Freelancer price and button visible\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  instead, and put the full explanations one scroll down.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Performance score:** Lighthouse reported 5–13 seconds of blocking time for both versions, which is\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  impossible for this page. It's noise from this machine, so the score says only that the two versions are\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  equal.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Reference comparison:** I compared against Basecamp, Linear and Stripe. FreshBooks wouldn't load. None\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  of the three answers visitors' worries or recommends a plan as directly. Stripe puts \"no hidden fees\" up\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  top, which backs that placement. Our page was weaker on one point: the buttons sat at the edge of an 800px\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  screen.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Fixed from the checks**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Button position:** I tightened the desktop spacing, so all three buttons now sit at 776px, inside an\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  800px screen.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Button alignment:** the Starter button had drifted 22px higher than the others, then 2px. I fixed both\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  and measured all three at 776px.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Cold-read problems:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - The \"logo and colors\" claim contradicted the Freelancer plan list.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - \"Flat monthly price\" clashed with yearly billing.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - Repeated \"no card needed\" lines are trimmed.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - The comparison table's groups are reorganised: Money, Looks professional, Your data, and Team & support.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Not verified**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - The final CSS fix for the pinned table column on phone wasn't rendered after I made it.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Lighthouse and the reference screenshots came from this machine and may differ on yours.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - I didn't test with real people, as you said.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  ▪ Step 6/8 done\u001b[0m\r\n"]
