[2686.722, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ **Stretch result: hit.** The page now puts the whole decision on a 390×700 phone screen, and I measured it\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  in a real 390px-wide frame.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Target and outcome**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Stretch target:** on a phone's first screen, all four worries answered with their explanation, and all\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  three plans identifiable by who they're for, with prices.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Fallback (my original target):** at least three worries answered and a plan pick in the first screen. It\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  stays passing on desktop, and now on phone as well.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Measured on the 390×700 phone:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - All four promise lines are fully in view.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - The toggle and all three plan rows, each with its price, are in view.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - The block ends at about 586px, leaving about 114px to spare.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - There is no horizontal overflow (375 of 390).\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - Desktop is unchanged: all four worries and the three \"Best for\" lines are still in view, and I confirmed\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  it in a render.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **What I built**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **One-line promises on phone:** \"No hidden fees · we never take a cut\", \"No lock-in · cancel in 2 clicks,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  export all\", \"Data safe · encrypted, daily backups\", and \"Looks pro · your logo; paid plans drop ours\".\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  These replace the four cards on phone and are hidden on desktop.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Plan rows:** \"Side projects, first clients → Starter $0\", \"Full-time freelancer → Freelancer $10/mo\"\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  (highlighted), and \"With subcontractors → Studio $24/mo\". Each links to its card, and the prices follow the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  billing toggle and currency.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Billing note:** I added one line under the plan rows, \"Per month, billed once a year\" (or \"billed\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  monthly\"), because showing \"$10/mo\" without it would hide the annual charge.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Card order:** with the plan rows doing the first-screen job, I put the plan cards back in natural order\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  (Starter, Freelancer, Studio) instead of Freelancer first.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Where it nearly broke**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Hidden note:** my first billing note was invisible because an older phone rule hid every paragraph in\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  the hero. I caught it by measuring its height at zero and scoped the rule to the subtitle only.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Fake failure:** my older worry-check reported \"false\" for the new copy because it ignores text nested in\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  bold labels. I relied on direct geometry checks of the new elements instead.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Not verified**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - I haven't looked at the final version after the billing-note fix. The earlier render looked right, and the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  later change adds one muted line.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - The phone shows \"Looks pro\", which is casual. You may prefer \"Looks professional\" at the cost of a longer\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  line.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  ▪ Step 7/8 done\u001b[0m\r\n"]
