[2780.963, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ The pricing page is finished: `pricing.html` now passes all 11 of the browser checks in `check-pricing.py`.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  It had no problems left to fix at the end. Your plan was to swap in your own prices and links later, so\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  those and three invented policy claims still need your input before launch.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **You asked for → it became**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Asked for:** a pricing page for a freelancer invoicing app, as a single web page.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Became:** a page where a freelancer picks a plan in about 10 seconds and sees the four worries answered\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  (hidden fees, lock-in, data safety, looking professional to clients) without hunting. You ranked those\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  worries first, then the 10-second pick, then polish.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **How each part was raised:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Plans:** each has a \"Best for\" line and a short reassurance under its button.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Billing and currency:** the toggle shows the real yearly charge and the savings, in three currencies.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Comparison table:** regrouped, with screen-reader text on every mark.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **FAQ:** ordered around the four worries.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Testimonial and call to action:** the fake \"40,000+\" claim is gone.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Billing strip:** a new \"What happens after you click\" strip under the plans.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Against the first version** (saved at `/tmp/ambition-first/pricing.v1.html`)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Check | First version | Final |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  |---|---|---|\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Worries answered in the first screen, desktop | 0 of 4 | 4 of 4, plus 3 \"Best for\" lines |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Phone first screen | no plan prices | all 4 promises and 3 plan rows with prices |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Browser checks passed | 5 of 11 | 11 of 11 |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Lighthouse accessibility, best practices, SEO | 100 | 100 |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Lighthouse performance | 62 | 62, with first paint at 1.0s against 1.5s |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **What it gave up:** on phones the four worry cards became one-line promises, and the comparison table\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  scrolls sideways with its feature column pinned.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Performance score:** Lighthouse measured seconds of blocking time for both versions, which is impossible\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  for this page. It reflects this loaded machine, so I treat it as equal, not as a real score.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Outside check:** `check-pricing.py` runs the page in headless Chrome and reads the real layout. It checks\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  the first screen on desktop and a 390×700 phone, overflow, prices in every currency and period, and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  accessibility basics. It passed 11 of 11 on the final page, and a Lighthouse run on the final page scored\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  100 for accessibility, best practices and SEO. I also compared the page against Basecamp, Linear and Stripe,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  and none of them answers visitors' worries or recommends a plan as directly. FreshBooks wouldn't load. I did\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  not test with real people, as you said.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Stretch:** the target was the whole decision on a phone's first screen: all four worries with their\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  explanation, and all three plans with prices. It got there, with about 114px to spare (the plan rows end\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  near 586px of 700). It nearly broke twice: a hidden billing note and a misleading check, both fixed. I\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  haven't looked at the final phone render after the last small change.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Locked in**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **`check-pricing.py`:** run `python3 -I check-pricing.py`. It prints PASS or FAIL lines, exits non-zero on\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  any failure, and also counts the `PLACEHOLDER` markers.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **`CLAUDE.md`:** says what to swap before launch and how to run the check.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **No project command:** a script is enough for this.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Assumptions I made** (you answered every question, so these are about content you hadn't specified)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Name and tiers:** the app is called \"Ledgerly\", with three plans at $0, $10 and $24 per month billed\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  yearly. EUR and GBP prices are fixed numbers I chose, not converted rates.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Policy claims:** the 14-day trial with no card, a 30-day money-back guarantee, 90 days of read-only\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  access after cancelling, and encryption with daily backups. None of these are real, and three are marked\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  `PLACEHOLDER` in the HTML: the testimonial, the data-protection claim and the billing strip.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Decisions left**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Owners and dates are my suggestions, and they're yours to change.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | # | Decision | Options and trade-offs | My pick | Owner, date |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  |---|---|---|---|---|\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | 1 | Confirm the policy claims (security, refund, 90-day read-only, trial emails) | **Keep as written:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  fast, but false claims would be a real harm. **Edit to your real terms:** slower, safe. | Edit to real\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  terms. This is the urgent one. | You (with legal if you have it), by 2026-12-01 |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | 2 | Real prices and tiers | **Keep three tiers:** clear and now tested. **Two tiers:** simpler, loses the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  team option. | Keep three tiers with your real prices. | You, by 2026-12-01 |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | 3 | Card up front or not for trials | **No card:** matches the page's promises and builds trust. **Card\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  required:** likely more paid conversions, but contradicts the page and needs edits in four places. | No\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  card, to match the page's promises. | You, by 2026-12-01 |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | 4 | Default billing period | **Yearly:** lower headline price. **Monthly:** simplest, no annual-charge\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  surprise. | Keep yearly, now with a darker billing line. | You, at launch |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | 5 | Replace the invented testimonial with a real quote, with permission | **Keep placeholder:** cheaper,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  but it's a fake claim. **Real quote:** takes asking a customer. | Real quote, as soon as you have one. |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  You, before launch |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Next check:** run `python3 -I check-pricing.py` after swapping in real prices and links, and again before\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  launch. Owner: whoever edits the page. Date: before launch.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Metrics**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  ```\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Metrics since 2026-11-24T12:01:37Z (cost: /cost, or total_cost_usd in headless JSON)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  total   in 194 · out 83.7k (think 26.9k) · cache read 7.73M · write 140.9k · hit 98% · 85 calls\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  model   sonnet-5-5: in 194 · out 83.7k (think 26.9k) · cache read 7.73M · write 140.9k · hit 98% · 85 calls\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  ```\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  ▪ Step 8/8 done\u001b[0m\r\n"]
